<title>FINLAND: VALMET JAN-AUG NET SALES BY DIVISION.</title>
<headline>VALMET JAN-AUG NET SALES BY DIVISION.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish paper machine maker and</p>
<p>engineering group Valmet Oy gave the following sales breakdown:</p>
<p>(million markka):</p>
<p> Net sales			Jan-Aug 1996	  Jan-Aug 1995</p>
<p> Paper and Board Machinery	6,133		   3,862</p>
<p> Automation			     861		     632</p>
<p> Automotive			     311		     279</p>
<p> Power Transmission		   229		     160</p>
<p> Others				     5			 5</p>
<p> Aviation Industries		  nil		     167</p>
<p> Intra group sales		   -175		     -97</p>
<p> TOTAL				  7,364		   5,008</p>
<p>At the start of 1996, Valmet started using a new so called</p>
<p>percentage of completion accounting method. This &quot;has a</p>
<p>significant impact on the net sales and operating profit figures</p>
<p>of the first two interim periods of 1996,&quot; Valmet said in a</p>
<p>statement.</p>
<p>With the accounting method in use last year, comparable</p>
<p>group net sales were 5.83 billion markka in January-August 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;Applying the percentage of completion method diminishes the</p>
<p>volatility between interim periods,&quot; Valmet said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 0 - 680 50 245</p>
</text>
